{
  "sn35.96:0.1": "Linked Discourses 35.96 ",
  "sn35.96:0.2": "10. The Sixes ",
  "sn35.96:0.3": "Liable to Decline ",
  "sn35.96:1.1": "“Mendicants, I will teach you who is liable to decline, who is not liable to decline, and the six fields of mastery. ",
  "sn35.96:1.2": "Listen … ",
  "sn35.96:1.3": "And how is someone liable to decline? ",
  "sn35.96:1.4": "When a mendicant sees a sight with their eyes, bad, unskillful phenomena arise: memories and thoughts that tighten the fetters. ",
  "sn35.96:1.5": "Suppose that mendicant tolerates them and doesn’t give them up, dispel them, eliminate them, and obliterate them. They should understand: ",
  "sn35.96:1.6": "‘My skillful qualities are declining. ",
  "sn35.96:1.7": "For this is what the Buddha calls decline.’ ",
  "sn35.96:2.1": "Furthermore, when a mendicant hears a sound … smells an odor … tastes a flavor … encounters a touch … ",
  "sn35.96:2.2": "knows an idea with their mind, bad, unskillful phenomena arise: memories and thoughts that tighten the fetters. ",
  "sn35.96:2.3": "If that mendicant tolerates them and doesn’t give them up, dispel them, eliminate them, and obliterate them, they should understand: ",
  "sn35.96:2.4": "‘My skillful qualities are declining. ",
  "sn35.96:2.5": "For this is what the Buddha calls decline.’ ",
  "sn35.96:2.6": "That’s how someone is liable to decline. ",
  "sn35.96:3.1": "And how is someone not liable to decline? ",
